WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.753
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.023 --> 00:08.723
I like her.

3
00:10.458 --> 00:14.471
I have feelings for Ms. Yeon Su.

4
00:21.290 --> 00:23.526
Have you lost your mind?

5
00:23.526 --> 00:25.238
What?

6
00:25.902 --> 00:27.238
Mom!

7
00:27.238 --> 00:29.026
It's nothing like that.

8
00:29.026 --> 00:32.046
Auntie! Nam Su! It really isn't. Okay?

9
00:32.046 --> 00:34.649
Please pretend you didn't hear that.

10
00:34.649 --> 00:36.535
- Excuse me... - Quiet!

11
00:39.682 --> 00:41.540
We need to talk.

12
00:51.010 --> 00:53.051
What was that just now?

13
00:53.958 --> 00:55.346
- A confession? - Why?

14
00:55.346 --> 00:56.922
Why do you think I confessed?

15
00:56.922 --> 00:59.617
- Obviously... - You obviously wanted to help me.

16
00:59.617 --> 01:01.119
I know that too.

17
01:01.119 --> 01:05.206
But you're basically making things worse for me!

18
01:05.206 --> 01:06.270
Look, Ms. Yeon Su...

19
01:06.270 --> 01:09.094
Do you know what confessing in front of my mom means?

20
01:09.094 --> 01:12.462
She'll hound me about whether we're dating.

21
01:12.462 --> 01:15.049
Grandma will call distant relatives.

22
01:15.049 --> 01:18.306
Then Grandpa will find out too!

23
01:18.306 --> 01:20.134
What were you possibly thinking?

24
01:20.134 --> 01:21.971
Of all the excuses you could've made, why on earth that one?

25
01:21.971 --> 01:24.426
- Let me say something. - Fine, go ahead.

26
01:24.426 --> 01:26.690
I'll admit the timing wasn't great.

27
01:26.690 --> 01:28.494
And yes, I was trying to help.

28
01:28.494 --> 01:32.138
But calling it an excuse hurts.

29
01:32.138 --> 01:34.843
You think I wanted to be in this position?

30
01:35.982 --> 01:39.870
Mr. Dokgo Dal, I just want to date someone normally.

31
01:39.870 --> 01:43.026
Without family interference or pressure to marry.

32
01:43.026 --> 01:46.054
Just the two of us, figuring things out together.

33
01:46.054 --> 01:49.486
I wondered how far these feelings that started physically could go.

34
01:49.486 --> 01:51.190
That's what I wanted to find out.

35
01:51.190 --> 01:52.995
Yeon Su!

36
02:07.166 --> 02:10.228
Father, Father! Father! Oh dear!

37
02:11.050 --> 02:13.469
Oh no, what do we do?

38
02:14.146 --> 02:15.302
Grandpa...

39
02:15.302 --> 02:17.152
What is all this commotion?

40
02:27.518 --> 02:29.662
Grandpa, well, you see...

41
02:29.662 --> 02:30.934
It's late.

42
02:30.934 --> 02:32.901
Go inside and get some sleep.

43
02:50.926 --> 02:55.202
You really have to watch what you say within these walls.

44
02:55.202 --> 02:56.598
I got caught getting divorced

45
02:56.598 --> 03:00.062
because I argued with that punk's lawyer in the backyard.

46
03:00.062 --> 03:02.334
Oh, God... How much did he hear?

47
03:02.334 --> 03:04.070
Not all of it, right?

48
03:04.070 --> 03:06.106
- Right, Auntie? - Yeon Su,

49
03:06.106 --> 03:08.918
don't you know Grandpa's three natural gifts?

50
03:08.918 --> 03:12.322
His strong teeth, sharp eyesight, and...

51
03:12.322 --> 03:13.798
- A full head of hair? - Keen hearing!

52
03:16.045 --> 03:18.785
What do I do?

53
03:20.966 --> 03:23.326
Should I just apologize first?

54
03:25.070 --> 03:27.074
- You shouldn't. - Why not?

55
03:27.074 --> 03:28.962
What did you even do wrong?

56
03:28.962 --> 03:30.914
Sleeping with someone you like?

57
03:30.914 --> 03:34.296
Or wanting to date freely?

58
03:36.526 --> 03:38.922
If you're going to grovel, you'd be better off fighting back.

59
03:38.922 --> 03:43.298
The moment you apologize, you'll be admitting you're in the wrong.

60
03:43.298 --> 03:45.282
Well, I feel bad for Dad, but...

61
03:45.282 --> 03:48.686
The one who strikes first takes control!

62
03:48.686 --> 03:52.350
I mean, I had no one on my side,

63
03:52.350 --> 03:53.998
but you do, right?

64
03:53.998 --> 03:55.700
You have him.

65
04:13.750 --> 04:16.142
This radish is finally getting good.

66
04:16.813 --> 04:19.266
The last batch was way too mushy.

67
04:19.266 --> 04:24.721
By the way, why were you tossing and turning all night?

68
04:28.482 --> 04:30.230
Yeon Su!

69
04:30.230 --> 04:32.062
About that man from last night...

70
04:33.466 --> 04:35.318
Grandpa,

71
04:35.318 --> 04:37.806
I won't make excuses.

72
04:37.806 --> 04:39.646
It's exactly what you saw yesterday.

73
04:39.646 --> 04:41.470
I...

74
04:44.330 --> 04:47.106
I like Mr. Mr. Dokgo Dal!

75
04:47.106 --> 04:49.298
D-Dokgo Dal? Isn't he...

76
04:49.298 --> 04:50.963
- Bring him here. - But,

77
04:50.963 --> 04:53.598
neither of us is thinking about marriage right now.

78
04:53.598 --> 04:57.342
I don't want to bring him here, and we're not at that stage yet.

79
04:57.342 --> 04:59.642
We just want to...

80
04:59.642 --> 05:01.738
date, no...

81
05:02.554 --> 05:05.595
We'll start with dating.

82
05:06.258 --> 05:08.934
I knew he was that kind of scoundrel.

83
05:08.934 --> 05:11.576
What? After getting you into...

84
05:14.114 --> 05:18.242
that whole situation, is he running off and leaving you alone?

85
05:18.242 --> 05:19.894
- Pardon? - He's clearly the type

86
05:19.894 --> 05:23.110
to take advantage of your innocent heart and dump you.

87
05:23.110 --> 05:25.062
And you want to do what with a guy like that?

88
05:25.062 --> 05:26.218
Date him?

89
05:26.218 --> 05:28.270
What kind of nonsense is that?

90
05:28.270 --> 05:29.865
T-That's not it, Grandpa.

91
05:29.865 --> 05:32.639
If not, bring him here without another word!

92
05:34.814 --> 05:35.970
I don't care about any of that!

93
05:35.970 --> 05:40.297
Quit your job and get married through a match before the year's out.

94
05:44.274 --> 05:46.002
Answer me!

95
05:46.770 --> 05:49.518
No, Grandpa.

96
05:49.518 --> 05:51.850
W-What did you say?

97
05:53.254 --> 05:57.698
Going along with what the elders want, regardless of my own wishes,

98
05:57.698 --> 06:01.202
I don't want to do that anymore.

99
06:01.202 --> 06:03.926
- Gong Yeon Su! - Are you defying me right now?

100
06:03.926 --> 06:05.966
I'm not defying you.

101
06:05.966 --> 06:10.366
I want to live my life on my own terms.

102
06:10.366 --> 06:12.170
Is that so?

103
06:15.450 --> 06:17.410
Then get out.

104
06:17.410 --> 06:20.029
If you're going to disgrace this family by doing whatever you want,

105
06:20.029 --> 06:21.782
then get out!

106
06:23.994 --> 06:25.906
Get out!

107
06:32.978 --> 06:35.442
[Episode 9]

108
06:35.442 --> 06:37.802
Why did you do that, Godal?

109
06:37.802 --> 06:40.074
- What? - You're a genius strategist.

110
06:40.074 --> 06:41.622
Remember how you made Loand a hit

111
06:41.622 --> 06:44.306
with talks and classes when it first opened?

112
06:44.306 --> 06:46.988
You're always thinking several moves ahead!

113
06:49.550 --> 06:53.286
So how could someone like you make a confession like that?

114
06:54.298 --> 06:56.978
You know what this means, right?

115
06:56.978 --> 06:58.258
I know.

116
06:58.258 --> 07:00.602
I put Gong Yeon Su in a difficult position.

117
07:00.602 --> 07:03.014
Now that the family knows about us,

118
07:03.014 --> 07:05.170
they'll start interfering for real.

119
07:05.170 --> 07:07.774
It's her grandpa, of all people.

120
07:07.774 --> 07:10.278
Do you think he'll stop at just interfering?

121
07:12.002 --> 07:15.867
Can you actually marry Gong Yeon Su?

122
07:18.658 --> 07:20.506
Do you get it now?

123
07:20.506 --> 07:25.378
Do you see what your impulsive confession has put Ms. Yeon Su through?

124
07:25.378 --> 07:27.702
I've played Go with her grandfather, so I know what he's like.

125
07:27.702 --> 07:30.790
He's ruthless with every move he makes.

126
07:30.790 --> 07:33.790
What if she's locked in a storeroom,

127
07:33.790 --> 07:36.658
without even a drop of water?

128
07:40.450 --> 07:42.460
I'm thirsty...

129
07:44.050 --> 07:46.534
- A storeroom? - One latte, please.

130
07:46.534 --> 07:47.778
Anything else?

131
07:47.778 --> 07:52.986
Excuse me, sorry to bother you, but I work at Loand on the fifth floor.

132
07:52.986 --> 07:55.930
Could you maybe...

133
07:55.930 --> 08:00.450
hold onto this for me until I get off work?

134
08:00.450 --> 08:03.538
I'm sorry, we don't mind smaller items,

135
08:03.538 --> 08:04.658
but a suitcase is a bit much...

136
08:04.658 --> 08:07.798
Oh, that's fine.

137
08:07.798 --> 08:08.904
I'm sorry to trouble you.

138
08:08.904 --> 08:10.150
I'm sorry.

139
08:10.150 --> 08:11.841
Your coffee will be right out.

140
08:11.841 --> 08:13.574
Oh, thanks.

141
08:41.614 --> 08:43.122
Did anything happen?

142
08:43.122 --> 08:45.682
No. Nothing, really.

143
08:45.682 --> 08:46.710
What about your grandpa?

144
08:46.710 --> 08:50.378
Well... he's fine too.

145
08:58.546 --> 09:02.062
Ugh, I drank too much yesterday, so my stomach hurts.

146
09:02.062 --> 09:04.410
I'll head up first. Grab my coffee, please.

147
09:04.410 --> 09:06.270
Okay.

148
09:07.658 --> 09:08.866
I'm sorry.

149
09:08.866 --> 09:12.062
- I got you into this mess. - Oh, no. Not at all.

150
09:12.062 --> 09:13.566
Did I put you in a tough spot?

151
09:13.566 --> 09:16.046
I said it's fine. Don't worry about it.

152
09:16.046 --> 09:17.538
I'll speak to your grandfather myself...

153
09:17.538 --> 09:19.442
I said no!

154
09:20.078 --> 09:23.082
This is between me and my family.

155
09:23.082 --> 09:29.002
So you don't need to feel responsible, Mr. Dokgo Dal.

156
09:29.002 --> 09:31.373
Here's your latte.

157
09:32.146 --> 09:33.422
Thank you.

158
09:33.422 --> 09:35.633
I'll head up first.

159
09:35.633 --> 09:37.333
- Okay. - Yeah.

160
09:41.238 --> 09:43.081
- What's wrong? - Huh?

161
09:45.478 --> 09:47.278
Nothing.

162
09:57.202 --> 10:00.942
Don't you dare let Yeon Su back in without my permission.

163
10:00.942 --> 10:03.346
She shouldn't be so distracted by a man.

164
10:03.346 --> 10:05.722
Nam Su, pull yourself together too!

165
10:05.722 --> 10:07.373
A daughter leaves the family upon marriage,

166
10:07.373 --> 10:09.774
but this family's honor falls entirely on you.

167
10:09.774 --> 10:13.820
If you cross the line like your sister, I won't let it slide, okay?

168
10:34.830 --> 10:36.850
Come here.

169
10:44.262 --> 10:46.222
What about your classes?

170
10:47.098 --> 10:48.654
I switched to evening classes.

171
10:48.654 --> 10:49.866
What do you do during the day?

172
10:49.866 --> 10:52.950
I work part-time during the day.

173
10:52.950 --> 10:55.354
And I thought I should help take care of Si Eun too.

174
10:55.354 --> 10:59.802
What, wasn't selling off the aged soy sauce enough?

175
10:59.802 --> 11:02.237
I've opened and closed those crocks for 30 years.

176
11:02.237 --> 11:04.554
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

177
11:08.422 --> 11:12.729
I should meet that girl.

178
11:21.178 --> 11:23.406
Did you hear back from JC?

179
11:24.045 --> 11:27.114
They offered us a short-term flagship store at Hyeonseong Department Store.

180
11:27.114 --> 11:30.038
If we meet the sales targets, they'll consider a long-term contract.

181
11:30.038 --> 11:34.082
They've left the store design and brand guidelines up to us.

182
11:34.082 --> 11:36.530
Then staffing and setup costs will be the issue.

183
11:36.530 --> 11:38.602
Unlike a pop-up, we'll have ongoing expenses.

184
11:38.602 --> 11:42.102
I thought we'd been told some funding would be available.

185
11:42.102 --> 11:44.082
I'll look into that.

186
11:44.082 --> 11:47.522
Alright, everyone! Could I have your attention for a moment?

187
11:47.522 --> 11:48.674
Guess what this is!

188
11:48.674 --> 11:49.962
What is it? A doll?

189
11:49.962 --> 11:54.458
Wrong! After six months of deliberation and endless Q&As, our very own Munch

190
11:54.458 --> 11:56.014
has finally made his first purchase!

191
11:56.014 --> 11:57.940
Everyone, applause!

192
11:58.638 --> 12:01.214
Oh, my! What's gotten into him?

193
12:01.214 --> 12:02.446
What did he buy?

194
12:02.446 --> 12:03.986
None other than...

195
12:03.986 --> 12:05.982
Dreaming! And the Pro version, no less!

196
12:05.982 --> 12:08.798
Wow, he went all out.

197
12:08.798 --> 12:10.690
Giving him those reward points paid off, huh?

198
12:10.690 --> 12:12.178
Tell him about the repeat-purchase promotion.

199
12:12.178 --> 12:14.333
- And throw in plenty of samples. - Got it.

200
12:14.333 --> 12:17.762
By the way, why put the product in this box? What happened to ours?

201
12:17.762 --> 12:19.173
I told you before.

202
12:19.173 --> 12:23.414
He specifically requested that his family never find out.

203
12:23.414 --> 12:25.350
A decoy box!

204
12:25.350 --> 12:27.574
That rabbit looks awfully determined.

205
12:28.605 --> 12:31.406
It's smooth sailing for him from now on!

206
12:31.406 --> 12:33.935
This should spice up his marriage.

207
12:55.378 --> 12:58.522
- You're Si Eun, right? - Yes.

208
12:58.522 --> 13:02.714
I know it couldn't have been easy to come, so thank you for coming.

209
13:02.714 --> 13:05.225
The reason I asked to meet today was...

210
13:05.225 --> 13:10.263
May I... go first?

211
13:11.826 --> 13:13.718
I...

212
13:14.626 --> 13:16.414
I can't marry him.

213
13:16.414 --> 13:19.462
I heard your family has soy sauce that's 200 years old.

214
13:19.462 --> 13:22.130
You hold 22 ancestral rites a year,

215
13:22.130 --> 13:24.018
and Nam Su is the eldest son.

216
13:24.018 --> 13:27.822
I can't see myself marrying into that family and spending my life

217
13:29.506 --> 13:31.594
just raising children.

218
13:31.594 --> 13:34.328
Nam Su is important to me, but...

219
13:34.982 --> 13:37.832
my own life matters more to me.

220
13:48.570 --> 13:50.694
Take this.

221
13:50.694 --> 13:55.822
Treat yourself to something nice, and use the rest for whatever you need.

222
13:55.822 --> 14:01.314
I can't presume to interfere in your relationship.

223
14:03.438 --> 14:07.445
And this is all I can do for you.

224
14:09.866 --> 14:11.582
I just

225
14:11.582 --> 14:17.662
hope you make the decision that's right for you.

226
14:17.662 --> 14:22.202
Whatever you decide, no one will blame you.

227
14:22.202 --> 14:24.112
Not even Nam Su.

228
14:25.014 --> 14:27.699
Because that's how I raised him.

229
14:34.494 --> 14:35.682
It's plum syrup.

230
14:35.682 --> 14:39.114
It turned out even better than the one Nam Su took.

231
14:39.114 --> 14:41.229
Nam Su...

232
14:41.974 --> 14:44.298
takes after you, ma'am.

233
14:44.942 --> 14:47.860
That's probably why he's so warm.

234
15:00.906 --> 15:03.602
Make sure she eats well. She looked so thin.

235
15:03.602 --> 15:05.598
Mom.

236
15:09.198 --> 15:11.146
I'm sorry...

237
15:11.838 --> 15:13.978
Gong Nam Su!

238
15:13.978 --> 15:16.338
I know you're shocked and confused,

239
15:16.338 --> 15:19.098
but you're not the one suffering the most.

240
15:19.098 --> 15:22.010
So pull yourself together and be there for her.

241
15:22.010 --> 15:23.874
Got it?

242
15:30.950 --> 15:32.905
I'm leaving.

243
15:35.038 --> 15:36.782
Get home safe.

244
15:55.886 --> 15:58.670
Well, look at our Gen Z employee!

245
15:58.670 --> 15:59.834
Wow!

246
15:59.834 --> 16:02.690
What's the occasion? Why are you so dressed up?

247
16:02.690 --> 16:05.006
Well... a graduation?

248
16:05.006 --> 16:06.086
Graduation?

249
16:06.086 --> 16:08.038
I'll be heading out now!

250
16:08.038 --> 16:09.706
Boss, I'll get going first!

251
16:09.706 --> 16:12.795
Well, I should get going too.

252
16:14.397 --> 16:16.030
Aren't you leaving, Ms. Gong?

253
16:18.046 --> 16:20.194
I still have some work to do. Go ahead.

254
16:20.194 --> 16:22.910
Alright, then. I'm off!

255
16:22.910 --> 16:25.082
- I'll get going! - See you.

256
16:26.894 --> 16:29.574
- Good work today. - Thanks...

257
16:30.830 --> 16:32.438
- I'm off. - Okay.

258
16:32.438 --> 16:34.283
Bye, see you.

259
16:48.893 --> 16:53.158
I have my final lesson with my little wolf today.

260
16:53.158 --> 16:55.918
I'll make sure he graduates looking his best.

261
16:55.918 --> 16:58.042
- Graduate? - But why'd you call?

262
16:59.037 --> 17:02.974
Did my mom happen to call you?

263
17:02.974 --> 17:04.966
No, why? What's going on with your mother?

264
17:04.966 --> 17:07.718
Well, the thing is...

265
17:07.718 --> 17:08.954
I...

266
17:08.954 --> 17:10.650
left home...

267
17:10.650 --> 17:11.890
Hold on.

268
17:11.890 --> 17:13.918
My little wolf's calling. Just a second.

269
17:13.918 --> 17:15.662
Let me call you back!

270
17:21.970 --> 17:24.582
Are you really going to do this?

271
17:24.582 --> 17:28.242
If you like each other, just tell him you're seeing each other seriously.

272
17:28.242 --> 17:30.042
That should reassure him.

273
17:30.042 --> 17:32.766
Do you have to defy him like this?

274
17:32.766 --> 17:34.170
I don't want that.

275
17:34.170 --> 17:37.882
I won't let my marriage become a way to keep the elders calm.

276
17:37.882 --> 17:42.186
I've dated behind your back and even dreamed of getting married.

277
17:42.186 --> 17:44.890
But it wasn't because I truly loved someone

278
17:44.890 --> 17:47.942
or had grown close to them.

279
17:47.942 --> 17:50.690
I just kept hearing that there's a right time to get married.

280
17:50.690 --> 17:52.862
And I let myself be dragged along.

281
17:52.862 --> 17:54.630
But...

282
17:56.766 --> 17:59.842
I don't want to do that anymore.

283
17:59.842 --> 18:01.794
At least when it comes to marriage,

284
18:01.794 --> 18:06.250
I want to truly like someone, get to know them, and fall in love.

285
18:06.250 --> 18:11.274
I want those feelings to grow until I know there's no one else for me.

286
18:11.274 --> 18:13.357
That's when I want to get married.

287
18:17.082 --> 18:18.982
I understand how you feel,

288
18:18.982 --> 18:22.230
but not upsetting your parents is also your filial duty.

289
18:22.230 --> 18:25.822
And this certainly won't convince your grandfather.

290
18:25.822 --> 18:27.926
Then what should I do?

291
18:27.926 --> 18:30.870
Drop to my knees and beg for forgiveness?

292
18:30.870 --> 18:32.350
Instead of living as Gong Yeon Su,

293
18:32.350 --> 18:36.638
should I just live as a marriageable daughter and granddaughter?

294
18:36.638 --> 18:38.061
Like you, Mom,

295
18:38.061 --> 18:41.719
who spent 30 years living only as a daughter-in-law of the Gong family?

296
18:45.730 --> 18:47.610
Mom,

297
18:48.266 --> 18:50.269
I'm sorry,

298
18:51.206 --> 18:53.773
but I won't live the way you did.

299
19:09.874 --> 19:15.005
[Mom...]

300
19:20.474 --> 19:24.210
[Studio building] Oh, the minimum rental period is a week.

301
19:24.210 --> 19:26.230
That's pretty expensive.

302
19:26.230 --> 19:27.698
It's dangerous around there.

303
19:27.698 --> 19:29.070
Oh! You startled me.

304
19:29.070 --> 19:31.294
That neighborhood gets pretty dark.

305
19:34.858 --> 19:37.186
Did you get kicked out of your house?

306
19:37.186 --> 19:38.922
No!

307
19:38.922 --> 19:42.366
It's not like that. More like... moving out on my own?

308
19:42.366 --> 19:43.502
Get out!

309
19:43.502 --> 19:48.718
Well, I was lightly nudged toward independence,

310
19:48.718 --> 19:50.818
but I walked out on my own feet,

311
19:50.818 --> 19:53.261
so I guess that counts as moving out.

312
19:53.938 --> 19:56.654
Yeon Su, I have your suitcase.

313
19:56.654 --> 19:58.671
What? You do?

314
20:00.890 --> 20:04.302
Ugh, I drank too much yesterday, so my stomach hurts.

315
20:04.302 --> 20:06.929
I'll head up first. Grab my coffee, please.

316
20:07.966 --> 20:12.445
You looked so helpless, so I rescued it and put it in my trunk.

317
20:13.254 --> 20:15.722
Oh, thank you so much.

318
20:15.722 --> 20:17.357
Wait here a moment.

319
20:17.357 --> 20:19.886
Wait, Mr. Yoon!

320
20:19.886 --> 20:21.062
Well...

321
20:21.062 --> 20:26.454
Please don't tell Mr. Dokgo Dal.

322
20:26.454 --> 20:27.694
I'll bring it right over.

323
20:27.694 --> 20:30.096
Thank you.

324
20:31.514 --> 20:34.164
What a relief.

325
20:59.734 --> 21:02.170
- What are you doing? - Just... thinking.

326
21:02.170 --> 21:03.738
About what?

327
21:03.738 --> 21:09.033
I appreciate your kindness, but I don't think this is right.

328
21:09.978 --> 21:11.206
Where are you going?

329
21:11.206 --> 21:12.902
I'll figure that out myself...

330
21:12.902 --> 21:16.749
What kind of idiot lets his girlfriend go out alone at this hour?

331
21:28.230 --> 21:30.930
It wasn't an excuse,

332
21:31.866 --> 21:34.886
when I said I liked you.

333
21:34.886 --> 21:37.714
I'm someone who doesn't expect much.

334
21:37.714 --> 21:40.202
The moment I start hoping for something,

335
21:40.202 --> 21:44.999
whether at work or with people, I risk getting hurt.

336
21:44.999 --> 21:46.630
But

337
21:46.630 --> 21:49.698
the way I've protected myself all my life

338
21:51.030 --> 21:54.330
keeps falling apart whenever I'm with you.

339
21:54.330 --> 21:58.524
I keep wondering about you, hoping for things,

340
22:00.938 --> 22:02.920
and feeling a little hurt...

341
22:03.978 --> 22:08.842
If this really is what it feels like to like someone,

342
22:10.610 --> 22:15.190
and if you're the exception in my life,

343
22:15.190 --> 22:19.687
I think taking the risk is worth letting myself fall apart.

344
22:21.886 --> 22:23.746
So...

345
22:26.918 --> 22:29.305
I really do like you.

346
22:46.914 --> 22:49.826
You take the second floor. I take the first floor.

347
22:49.826 --> 22:52.278
The towels are in the bathroom.

348
22:52.278 --> 22:55.139
And I'll bring you a new toothbrush.

349
22:56.362 --> 22:58.382
We could share... the bed,

350
22:59.294 --> 23:02.771
if you want.

351
23:07.314 --> 23:11.672
We're not just friends anymore.

352
23:14.658 --> 23:18.370
Girl... friends with benefits?

353
23:22.034 --> 23:23.962
There's one thing

354
23:24.626 --> 23:27.504
I haven't told you...

355
23:28.174 --> 23:30.158
You snore.

356
23:30.850 --> 23:32.666
Do you have hair conditioner at home?

357
23:32.666 --> 23:35.287
My hair gets tangled easily.

358
23:45.430 --> 23:48.318
[Eggs]

359
23:48.318 --> 23:49.670
Do you have eggs?

360
23:49.670 --> 23:51.438
No.

361
23:55.646 --> 23:57.993
- Dried seaweed? - No.

362
24:01.114 --> 24:02.874
You have rice, right?

363
24:02.874 --> 24:05.850
Then you don't even have a rice cooker?

364
24:07.420 --> 24:08.468
A bit much, isn't it?

365
24:08.468 --> 24:09.474
Very much so.

366
24:09.474 --> 24:13.301
You need something filling in the morning.

367
24:13.301 --> 24:16.358
At least some soy sauce and egg over rice.

368
24:16.358 --> 24:19.807
That's how you get your brain going.

369
24:22.798 --> 24:25.002
Are we going to survival camp or something?

370
24:25.002 --> 24:29.370
It looks like a lot, but we'll use it up in no time.

371
24:30.443 --> 24:33.112
I forgot to buy groceries for dinner.

372
24:36.866 --> 24:39.660
None of this is for dinner?

373
24:40.378 --> 24:42.538
Shall we have dumplings?

374
24:51.726 --> 24:53.882
So, what time do you usually go to bed?

375
24:54.518 --> 24:56.978
- Around one or two? - O-One or two?

376
24:56.978 --> 24:59.090
Why?

377
24:59.090 --> 25:04.018
I usually go to bed at 11, midnight at the latest.

378
25:04.018 --> 25:06.126
Two is way too late.

379
25:06.126 --> 25:08.258
I have a bit of insomnia.

380
25:08.258 --> 25:11.550
I tend to sleep with the lights on too.

381
25:21.070 --> 25:24.086
Why don't you at least call them?

382
25:24.086 --> 25:26.046
They're probably really worried about you.

383
25:26.046 --> 25:29.714
And it's weighing on you too, isn't it?

384
25:29.714 --> 25:32.296
Who? Me?

385
25:33.718 --> 25:37.334
I feel completely free and comfortable right now.

386
25:37.334 --> 25:40.914
"Women and dishes should never leave the house."

387
25:40.914 --> 25:44.022
I grew up hearing things like that.

388
25:44.022 --> 25:48.395
I've been told to get married since my college entrance ceremony.

389
25:52.038 --> 25:54.466
Actually...

390
25:54.466 --> 25:56.170
I've always been afraid.

391
25:56.170 --> 26:01.238
Afraid I'd end up living like nothing more than a dish.

392
26:01.238 --> 26:05.754
I got into marketing to protect myself too.

393
26:05.754 --> 26:08.957
I thought seeing the world differently

394
26:08.957 --> 26:12.336
might someday give me the courage to take a chance.

395
26:17.558 --> 26:22.150
Anyway, long story short! This is definitely the boldest thing I've ever done.

396
26:22.150 --> 26:24.890
But I don't regret it!

397
26:25.746 --> 26:27.978
I won't impose on you for too long.

398
26:27.978 --> 26:31.162
I can stay at Sera's place while looking for an apartment.

399
26:31.162 --> 26:33.138
- Who said you could? - What?

400
26:33.138 --> 26:36.110
I mean, who's going to eat all those groceries?

401
26:36.110 --> 26:38.618
If you're leaving, finish all of it first.

402
26:39.805 --> 26:41.170
Don't worry.

403
26:41.170 --> 26:43.784
We'll finish it in no time.

404
26:49.026 --> 26:50.802
It's good.

405
27:23.882 --> 27:26.366
[Well-cooked sunny-side up egg] Rice, scallions, egg, soy sauce...

406
27:26.366 --> 27:27.758
[Top it onto the rice and done!] That's it?

407
27:27.758 --> 27:29.882
Easy enough.

408
27:29.882 --> 27:32.332
The egg is the tricky part.

409
27:34.090 --> 27:36.545
Why am I watching so intently?

410
27:46.038 --> 27:48.390
Does it really need butter?

411
27:53.230 --> 27:55.482
Oh, well...

412
27:55.482 --> 27:57.817
I just wanted some water.

413
27:59.550 --> 28:01.302
Okay.

414
28:45.618 --> 28:47.730
I guess...

415
28:47.730 --> 28:49.086
this day really did come.

416
28:49.086 --> 28:51.962
It wasn't anything special, but we had fun, didn't we?

417
28:51.962 --> 28:54.439
It wasn't the time that was special.

418
28:55.050 --> 28:57.067
You were the special one.

419
28:59.286 --> 29:03.530
You've really mastered the art of being a charming younger guy.

420
29:03.530 --> 29:05.366
I've had a great time with you.

421
29:05.366 --> 29:07.254
Now it's time to graduate.

422
29:07.254 --> 29:09.038
Thank you.

423
29:09.038 --> 29:11.746
Thanks to you, I don't resent anyone anymore.

424
29:11.746 --> 29:14.226
Who did you resent?

425
29:15.146 --> 29:20.774
Well, my ex, for one... and the women I almost dated.

426
29:21.466 --> 29:23.218
I was pretty pathetic.

427
29:23.218 --> 29:25.022
Min Hyeong,

428
29:25.766 --> 29:29.986
you think sex is all about

429
29:29.986 --> 29:32.046
that one physical act, right?

430
29:32.046 --> 29:35.578
But when you read your partner's signals, communicate,

431
29:35.578 --> 29:38.214
and share sensations,

432
29:38.214 --> 29:42.194
you learn about yourself as well as the other person.

433
29:42.194 --> 29:45.770
What you enjoy,

434
29:45.770 --> 29:49.494
and how you connect.

435
29:50.758 --> 29:55.426
The reason you've lacked confidence all this time

436
29:55.426 --> 29:58.470
was that you didn't really know yourself.

437
30:00.698 --> 30:02.542
I didn't do anything.

438
30:02.542 --> 30:04.893
You did it all yourself.

439
30:14.162 --> 30:16.269
The subscriber you dialed...

440
30:18.394 --> 30:20.218
- The subscriber you dialed... - Si Eun.

441
30:20.218 --> 30:23.638
You're not home, and you're not answering your phone. Where are you?

442
30:23.638 --> 30:25.994
Please pick up.

443
30:25.994 --> 30:28.283
We promised to talk everything through together.

444
31:01.938 --> 31:03.844
Hello?

445
31:06.850 --> 31:08.522
How's Grandpa?

446
31:08.522 --> 31:11.462
Is he... really mad?

447
31:11.462 --> 31:14.198
How's Mom?

448
31:14.198 --> 31:15.774
Your mom?

449
31:15.774 --> 31:18.030
She doesn't even flinch.

450
31:18.030 --> 31:20.302
Nothing gets to her.

451
31:20.914 --> 31:23.706
So don't worry about us.

452
31:23.706 --> 31:26.506
Just focus on your little rebellion.

453
31:26.506 --> 31:28.350
Okay.

454
31:28.350 --> 31:30.942
I'll call you again, Auntie.

455
31:57.178 --> 31:59.441
[Mom]

456
32:54.606 --> 32:56.278
Something came up, so I left early.

457
32:56.278 --> 32:58.099
Make sure you eat.

458
33:02.246 --> 33:06.333
Oh, come on. That's cute.

459
33:08.441 --> 33:10.295
Looks good!

460
33:19.934 --> 33:21.864
Salty...

461
33:36.526 --> 33:39.213
My fortune says

462
33:39.213 --> 33:41.250
disaster awaits me in my later years.

463
33:41.250 --> 33:44.754
To me, you are that disaster.

464
33:44.754 --> 33:47.422
Could that mean wealth instead of disaster?

465
33:47.422 --> 33:50.526
My chart is full of metal, so I'm destined for wealth.

466
33:50.526 --> 33:52.190
Wealth without virtue is no blessing.

467
33:52.190 --> 33:55.302
A man must first master himself and his household.

468
33:55.302 --> 33:57.962
A gentleman upholds righteousness and loyalty.

469
33:57.962 --> 34:01.418
If you don't even know moral principles, how can you call yourself a man?

470
34:07.342 --> 34:09.410
As they say, a gentleman must tend to his roots.

471
34:09.410 --> 34:11.834
Perseverance can wear away stone.

472
34:11.834 --> 34:15.114
And sincerity can move the heavens.

473
34:15.114 --> 34:18.701
Surely, the heavens will recognize my intentions too.

474
34:19.750 --> 34:21.874
Enough! What brings you here?

475
34:21.874 --> 34:24.258
I'm here to put Ms. Yeon Su's mind at ease.

476
34:24.258 --> 34:26.330
Why come here to put her mind at ease?

477
34:26.330 --> 34:28.934
She walked out of this house!

478
34:28.934 --> 34:31.402
Because her heart is still here.

479
34:31.402 --> 34:32.658
Wh-What?

480
34:32.658 --> 34:36.034
Your approval isn't everything to me, sir.

481
34:36.034 --> 34:39.514
Even if you disapprove of me, feelings matter more to me.

482
34:39.514 --> 34:42.018
But Ms. Yeon Su is different.

483
34:42.018 --> 34:43.325
Even if she's with me,

484
34:43.325 --> 34:47.142
she can only be happy if you and the family accept us.

485
34:48.750 --> 34:50.838
Would you please

486
34:50.838 --> 34:53.256
give us your blessing to date?

487
34:57.110 --> 35:01.286
You're stirring up my feelings just to put hers at ease?

488
35:01.286 --> 35:03.738
With all due respect,

489
35:03.738 --> 35:06.982
sometimes you have to stir things up to uncover the truth.

490
35:06.982 --> 35:08.872
Like, for instance...

491
35:09.510 --> 35:12.861
how much you love your granddaughter.

492
35:14.586 --> 35:17.530
I... don't like you.

493
35:17.530 --> 35:19.485
My approval isn't everything to you anyway,

494
35:19.485 --> 35:22.010
so you don't mind hearing that, right?

495
35:22.686 --> 35:26.498
May I ask what you don't like about me?

496
35:26.498 --> 35:32.078
First! Your cowardly habit of dressing up irresponsibility as caution.

497
35:32.078 --> 35:34.754
Second! You're too tall.

498
35:34.754 --> 35:37.025
And third, the biggest issue!

499
35:38.882 --> 35:40.802
I heard you're shooting blanks!

500
35:40.802 --> 35:43.030
What? Blanks?

501
35:43.030 --> 35:45.166
I have azoospermia.

502
35:45.166 --> 35:48.506
I'll probably never have children in my life.

503
35:48.506 --> 35:50.686
- Well, that's... - You can go now.

504
35:50.686 --> 35:52.934
- Wait, sir... - Mi Young!

505
35:52.934 --> 35:55.327
See our guest out!

506
35:56.570 --> 35:59.406
This isn't personal...

507
35:59.406 --> 36:01.291
You know that, right?

508
36:05.610 --> 36:08.181
Toss the salt harder!

509
36:10.698 --> 36:12.886
Sorry.

510
36:18.522 --> 36:20.635
This isn't easy.

511
36:25.946 --> 36:27.859
Wait.

512
36:30.778 --> 36:34.274
Could we talk for a minute?

513
36:36.046 --> 36:39.738
Yeon Su left home.

514
36:40.998 --> 36:42.907
You know that, right?

515
36:44.430 --> 36:47.120
Do you know where she is?

516
36:49.294 --> 36:51.882
I heard she's staying with a senior she's close to.

517
36:51.882 --> 36:54.230
That's what I heard.

518
36:58.798 --> 37:00.717
It's all my fault.

519
37:01.426 --> 37:04.238
I was so busy being this family's daughter-in-law,

520
37:04.238 --> 37:08.446
I failed to see what my own child was going through.

521
37:08.446 --> 37:13.150
She swallowed everything without ever once saying no.

522
37:13.150 --> 37:16.191
So it must've all built up inside her.

523
37:18.510 --> 37:20.653
That just shows how strong Ms. Yeon Su is.

524
37:20.653 --> 37:23.406
Strong enough to endure all those years.

525
37:25.174 --> 37:27.458
She is a wise woman.

526
37:27.458 --> 37:30.302
She knows how to make the choices

527
37:30.302 --> 37:33.082
that are right for her.

528
37:35.398 --> 37:37.490
So, ma'am,

529
37:37.490 --> 37:39.547
you haven't failed her.

530
37:40.206 --> 37:42.509
You've been holding your family together.

531
37:47.502 --> 37:51.806
Can I trust you, Mr. Dokgo Dal?

532
37:51.806 --> 37:55.188
Please trust your daughter's choice.

533
37:58.558 --> 38:00.754
He went back to that house? At that hour?

534
38:00.754 --> 38:04.130
They seem pretty close, but the mood there is...

535
38:04.130 --> 38:05.174
What's wrong with the mood?

536
38:05.174 --> 38:08.158
I heard the old man there isn't

537
38:08.158 --> 38:09.914
too fond of your son.

538
38:09.914 --> 38:11.370
What's wrong with my son?

539
38:11.370 --> 38:13.206
How should I know?

540
38:13.206 --> 38:15.906
Ask him directly about this stuff from now on.

541
38:15.906 --> 38:18.630
If only he'd answer my calls...

542
38:18.630 --> 38:19.738
Anyway, got it.

543
38:19.738 --> 38:21.570
I'll call you again.

544
38:25.026 --> 38:27.498
Let's go to his office.

545
38:27.498 --> 38:29.862
No, wait. Let's go to his place.

546
38:29.862 --> 38:31.734
Yes, sir.

547
38:32.422 --> 38:35.079
[Dakgalbi cooking up deliciously] Cooked by...

548
38:35.079 --> 38:39.115
It's cooked in the residual heat.

549
39:31.718 --> 39:33.503
[Dokgo Dal]

550
39:36.214 --> 39:38.266
Where have you been all this...

551
39:52.286 --> 39:55.210
- Are you two living together? - No, absolutely not.

552
39:55.210 --> 39:56.902
It's just... Well...

553
39:56.902 --> 40:00.522
I-I can see how it might look that way...

554
40:00.522 --> 40:02.634
But it's really nothing like that!

555
40:02.634 --> 40:05.627
I'm just staying here temporarily due to some personal circumstances.

556
40:05.627 --> 40:07.612
So you are living together.

557
40:11.354 --> 40:14.702
Have you eaten yet?

558
40:15.514 --> 40:18.514
If you like cheonggukjang...

559
40:20.138 --> 40:21.674
Listen here.

560
40:21.674 --> 40:24.462
Do you think I came all this way just to have a meal?

561
40:26.606 --> 40:29.609
It tastes just like my maternal grandma's cooking.

562
40:34.738 --> 40:36.398
Does it suit your taste?

563
40:36.398 --> 40:38.367
It's really delicious...

564
40:46.614 --> 40:49.382
Does your family know you are here?

565
40:49.382 --> 40:52.770
No, they don't.

566
40:52.770 --> 40:54.802
Are you going to marry Dal?

567
40:56.317 --> 40:58.998
We're not quite at that stage yet.

568
40:58.998 --> 41:00.306
Why does there need to be a stage?

569
41:00.306 --> 41:01.494
Just get married.

570
41:01.494 --> 41:04.774
Oh, marriage is one of life's biggest decisions, right?

571
41:04.774 --> 41:08.464
It's not something you can do two or three times.

572
41:12.370 --> 41:13.790
Of course!

573
41:13.790 --> 41:16.206
That doesn't mean it's totally impossible...

574
41:16.206 --> 41:22.665
I just think once is probably enough for most people...

575
41:23.354 --> 41:25.162
Yeah.

576
41:26.114 --> 41:28.670
I'm sorry.

577
41:28.670 --> 41:30.018
I'd like to ask you a favor.

578
41:30.018 --> 41:31.714
Yes, please go ahead.

579
41:31.714 --> 41:35.986
Get him to wrap up the business he's running.

580
41:35.986 --> 41:38.758
- Pardon? - You two seem pretty serious.

581
41:38.758 --> 41:40.925
If you're going to get married someday,

582
41:40.925 --> 41:43.194
he should quit that business.

583
41:43.194 --> 41:45.266
He's capable and smart.

584
41:45.266 --> 41:50.474
Don't you think it's a waste of his talents to be doing that?

585
41:53.030 --> 41:55.214
Sir,

586
41:55.214 --> 41:58.717
you trust your son's abilities,

587
41:58.717 --> 42:01.762
but not his choices.

588
42:01.762 --> 42:05.098
You acknowledge what he's capable of, right?

589
42:05.098 --> 42:10.743
Then shouldn't you trust the choices he's made with those abilities?

590
42:50.086 --> 42:53.417
Why can't someone who's just sitting around at home do it?

591
42:53.417 --> 42:56.526
Why do I have to be out here doing chores at this hour?

592
42:56.526 --> 42:57.938
Jeez!

593
42:57.938 --> 42:59.786
Whether someone comes home or not,

594
42:59.786 --> 43:03.871
all he does is lie in bed sleeping all day!

595
43:10.962 --> 43:12.922
Good grief.

596
43:19.154 --> 43:21.230
Why is this...

597
43:21.230 --> 43:24.660
After six months of deliberation and endless Q&As, our very own Munch

598
43:24.660 --> 43:26.105
has finally made his first purchase!

599
43:26.105 --> 43:30.134
He specifically requested that his family never find out.

600
43:30.134 --> 43:31.693
A decoy box!

601
43:33.585 --> 43:34.969
[My wife and I are sexless. Will this really help our sex life?]

602
43:34.969 --> 43:36.474
[I lack the courage to give it to my wife. Please disguise the box thoroughly]

603
43:36.474 --> 43:38.615
Munch?

604
43:46.366 --> 43:48.222
You're back?

605
43:57.478 --> 43:59.726
Where have you been all day?

606
43:59.726 --> 44:01.696
You didn't even call.

607
44:02.822 --> 44:05.866
I went to meet someone. I also stopped by the factory.

608
44:05.866 --> 44:07.568
Who did you meet?

609
44:09.334 --> 44:14.030
Well... I just wondered when you'd be home and if you'd eaten.

610
44:14.030 --> 44:17.862
You could at least consider the person waiting at home.

611
44:20.934 --> 44:21.934
You missed me?

612
44:21.934 --> 44:26.662
I made two servings of cheonggukjang, but there was no one here to eat it.

613
44:28.082 --> 44:31.294
Actually, today... I went to see Grandfather.

614
44:31.294 --> 44:35.171
Oh, you have a grandfather too, Mr. Dokgo Dal?

615
44:37.162 --> 44:39.806
Wait. Don't tell me...

616
44:39.806 --> 44:40.966
Why would you do that?

617
44:40.966 --> 44:44.010
I left home so you wouldn't go to my house!

618
44:44.010 --> 44:46.766
Why would you go there without telling me?

619
44:48.190 --> 44:50.995
I'm getting scolded all day today.

620
44:53.358 --> 44:56.108
Did he give you a hard time?

621
45:01.618 --> 45:06.798
I think I understand now why you could never

622
45:06.798 --> 45:08.186
stand up to your grandfather.

623
45:08.186 --> 45:11.332
Why else do you think I ran away from home?

624
45:22.818 --> 45:26.514
- Why? - Nothing. I just think you're admirable.

625
45:29.642 --> 45:31.050
Shall we have dinner?

626
45:31.050 --> 45:32.858
You said you made cheonggukjang, right?

627
45:32.858 --> 45:35.398
Oh... it's already gone.

628
45:35.398 --> 45:37.750
Two servings? By yourself?

629
45:37.750 --> 45:39.522
With your dad.

630
45:39.522 --> 45:41.306
What?

631
45:42.762 --> 45:44.602
What?

632
45:44.602 --> 45:46.122
He just showed up out of nowhere.

633
45:46.122 --> 45:48.514
You did this without even telling me.

634
45:48.514 --> 45:50.834
He barged in without telling me, so what was I supposed to do?

635
45:50.834 --> 45:55.098
He hadn't eaten, and the cheonggukjang was ready.

636
45:55.098 --> 45:57.479
What did he want this time?

637
45:57.479 --> 45:59.421
Why was he here?

638
46:00.890 --> 46:02.922
Maybe he was worried.

639
46:02.922 --> 46:06.758
Maybe he loves his son?

640
46:08.086 --> 46:10.230
Don't be so hard on your dad.

641
46:10.230 --> 46:11.981
He may struggle to express it,

642
46:11.981 --> 46:14.574
but no parent is bad at loving their child.

643
46:14.574 --> 46:18.210
Then you should go talk things out with your grandfather too.

644
46:18.210 --> 46:20.726
He's just not good at showing how he feels.

645
46:20.726 --> 46:24.626
My grandfather isn't bad at expressing it. He's just set in his ways.

646
46:24.626 --> 46:28.927
There's a 30-year gap between someone in their 50s and someone in their 80s.

647
46:28.927 --> 46:33.374
A parent's love for their child knows no age or time.

648
46:33.374 --> 46:34.702
Don't you agree?

649
46:34.702 --> 46:37.197
I'll head upstairs first.

650
46:41.018 --> 46:43.154
Stay a little longer.

651
46:43.154 --> 46:45.134
I'm bored.

652
47:04.482 --> 47:06.342
[Mom] Answer it.

653
47:08.882 --> 47:10.142
I don't want to.

654
47:10.142 --> 47:13.271
She's worried. Just answer it.

655
47:17.186 --> 47:19.022
I'll head upstairs first.

656
47:19.022 --> 47:20.802
Okay.

657
47:44.954 --> 47:46.829
Are you asleep?

658
47:49.054 --> 47:51.334
Not yet.

659
47:51.334 --> 47:53.869
Is it because of the lights?

660
48:33.998 --> 48:37.163
I'm sorry. I can't do this.

661
48:42.197 --> 48:44.295
Y-You scared me...

662
48:45.834 --> 48:47.923
Let's stay together.

663
48:54.442 --> 48:56.599
I'll be here for you.

664
51:55.874 --> 51:58.122
[Be yourself!]

665
52:16.342 --> 52:19.934
Starting tomorrow, let's sleep upstairs together.

666
52:19.934 --> 52:22.429
The couch is nice and all,

667
52:23.050 --> 52:25.182
but it's a little cramped.

668
52:31.422 --> 52:33.157
Alright.

669
52:36.842 --> 52:39.071
Wait, who's here at this hour?

670
52:41.286 --> 52:42.654
Could it be Mr. Yoon?

671
52:42.654 --> 52:45.318
No, that can't be.

672
52:48.642 --> 52:50.402
Sera?

673
52:50.402 --> 52:54.102
Why is she here? How did she...

674
52:54.102 --> 52:56.046
The CEO of SR?

675
52:56.694 --> 52:57.882
I don't know. I swear.

676
52:57.882 --> 52:59.582
Wait...

677
52:59.582 --> 53:02.319
Why would she come here?

678
53:06.994 --> 53:10.160
Sera, what brings you here?

679
53:25.242 --> 53:27.954
M-Mom!
